    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4898037_9471cc5b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 37053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-24T07:39:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For some experimental pipelines we currently have a job that all other jobs are dependent on, which runs first and makes it possible to select which other jobs in the pipeline should run, with zuul_return and child_jobs. Could that type of functionality be implemented here, so selection of jobs in the pipeline is possible in the UI?\n\nIf job selection is moved into the web ui, it opens the opportunity to only display parameters relevant for the selected job/jobs, mapping the frozen job vars with the parameters for example.\n\nIf not we would still be able to use a similar solution as we have with experimental for job selection, but if that approach is used there would possibly be many parameters in the ui that are not relevant for the selected job.",
      "revId": "5cec65e6ccd6bd25ec926038de2471f0f2c53eda",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "39fe3ed1_73cd428f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-25T00:05:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That sounds like a good idea.  I\u0027m going to mark this comment thread as unresolved so I remember to add that in a future revision.",
      "parentUuid": "f1fbb006_93e55421",
      "revId": "5cec65e6ccd6bd25ec926038de2471f0f2c53eda",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e95e616_f01133f2",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-25T00:05:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Selecting jobs in the UI is somewhat in opposition to our goal for repeatability and also the way we define workflows in pipelines; we\u0027re still trying to be a project gating system first and foremost, not a general purpose job runner.  So I think that we should still expect people to define workflows using pipelines, etc.\n\nBut having said that, yes, you should still be able to have a dispatch job, and you will be able to use variables supplied through the web UI as input to that job, so you can make a construct to choose the appropriate jobs.  If that ends up having too many unrelated parameters, I would seriously recommend looking at adding pipelines based on workflow needs.\n\nIf I\u0027m wrong about this and we decide we need to add job selection in the web UI later, I don\u0027t think anything about this current proposal would prevent that.",
      "parentUuid": "a4898037_9471cc5b",
      "revId": "5cec65e6ccd6bd25ec926038de2471f0f2c53eda",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "60d9c1d4_b39d92a6",
        "filename": "doc/source/developer/specs/parameterized-builds.rst",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 4146
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-26T01:24:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One consequence of this change is that Zuul could theoretically be configured to be a more generic action taker system. Like Ansible Tower? I don\u0027t know that this is necessarily a bad thing, but it is worth considering how and if this may shift some of the identity of the system and how we approach problem solving within it.",
      "revId": "5cec65e6ccd6bd25ec926038de2471f0f2c53eda",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "980df645_d8a367b5",
        "filename": "doc/source/developer/specs/parameterized-builds.rst",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-26T01:31:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree it\u0027s a risk and I don\u0027t want to do that.  I think we should agree that it is not our intent.  There are a few things in this spec that discourage that (like still tying queue items to git refs, and workflow pipeline definitions).\n\nMaybe I should revise the spec to explicitly state the intention not to change the fundamental identity of the system.  I see it as expanding to cover an edge case that is related to software development that we did not (and could not have) had in OpenStack.",
      "parentUuid": "60d9c1d4_b39d92a6",
      "revId": "5cec65e6ccd6bd25ec926038de2471f0f2c53eda",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a9de221_f6a5958a",
        "filename": "doc/source/developer/specs/parameterized-builds.rst",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 150,
      "author": {
        "id": 4146
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-26T01:24:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m wondering if we would consider this valid for any pipeline. And in the case where a project has not defined any parameters I guess we would end up with a frozen config that doesn\u0027t want any parameters and the enqueue wouldn\u0027t be any different than what is possible today when enqueing builds without parameters?\n\nOr would we try to limit it specifically to special pipelines that are configured to accept parameters? I think this may end up being less confusing to users, but also potentially less functional since the alternative described above is a bit more flexible.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 150,
        "startChar": 51,
        "endLine": 150,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "5cec65e6ccd6bd25ec926038de2471f0f2c53eda",
